<section id="why" class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-[#0D1017] border-b border-slate-dark">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center mb-12 sm:mb-16">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-terminal border border-slate-dark text-xs font-mono text-cyber mb-4 uppercase tracking-wider">
        Why NightMe
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-6">
        Your agents can change. Your workflow doesn't have to.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate max-w-3xl mx-auto text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Claude Code today. Codex tomorrow. A different agent for the next task. NightMe keeps the way you work consistent while letting you choose the agent that fits the job.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-10 sm:mb-12">
      <div class="bg-terminal border border-slate-dark rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h3 class="text-cyber font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-bold mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">Agent-agnostic by design</h3>
        <p class="text-slate text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
          NightMe does not lock your workflow to one vendor, one model, or one remote-control app. It connects the local agents you already use to the same conversation and control layer.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto mb-10 sm:mb-12">
      <div class="text-center text-cyber font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-bold mb-4 uppercase tracking-wider">
        Mental model
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2 sm:gap-3 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <span class="bg-night border border-slate-dark rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-white">Conversation</span>
        <span class="text-cyber font-bold">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="bg-night border border-slate-dark rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-white">Project</span>
        <span class="text-cyber font-bold">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="bg-night border border-slate-dark rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-white">Persistent Session</span>
        <span class="text-cyber font-bold">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="bg-night border-2 border-cyber rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-cyber font-bold">Agent</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center text-slate text-sm sm:text-base italic leading-relaxed">
      Not another AI model. Not another coding environment. NightMe is the control layer between your conversations and the coding agents running on your machine.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>


<section id="chat-native" class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-night border-b border-slate-dark">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center mb-10 sm:mb-14">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-terminal border border-slate-dark text-xs font-mono text-cyber mb-4 uppercase tracking-wider">
        Chat-native, not another app
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-6">
        Code in the conversations you already use.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate max-w-3xl mx-auto text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        No new mobile IDE. No proprietary chat client to learn. Use a supported IM app you already know to talk to your local coding agents through NightMe.
      </p>
    </div>

    
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-10 sm:mb-14 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="bg-terminal border border-slate-dark rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-6">
        <div class="text-cyber font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-bold mb-2 uppercase tracking-wider">Keep your familiar workflow</div>
        <p class="text-slate text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Send instructions and review responses using the chat experience you already understand.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-terminal border border-slate-dark rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-6">
        <div class="text-cyber font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-bold mb-2 uppercase tracking-wider">No app lock-in</div>
        <p class="text-slate text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
          NightMe is designed to work across supported chat platforms instead of forcing you into a single messaging product.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-terminal border border-slate-dark rounded-xl p-5 sm:p-6">
        <div class="text-cyber font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-bold mb-2 uppercase tracking-wider">Stay informed without babysitting</div>
        <p class="text-slate text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Statusbar and reaction signals keep you updated while the local agent keeps working.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    
    <div class="text-center mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-white text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold">Inside one conversation</h3>
      <p class="text-slate text-xs sm:text-sm mt-2">Every message routes to the local agent in the right project, and replies come back with full context.</p>
    </div>

