<section id="persistent" class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-[#0D1017] border-b border-slate-dark">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center mb-10 sm:mb-14">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-terminal border border-slate-dark text-xs font-mono text-cyber mb-4 uppercase tracking-wider">
        Persistent sessions
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-6">
        Your coding sessions stay alive.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate max-w-3xl mx-auto text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Close the terminal. Leave the desk. Come back later. Your NightMe session stays tied to its project so you can continue the same work instead of starting over from a blank context.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
      <div class="bg-terminal border border-slate-dark rounded-xl p-6">
        <div class="text-cyber font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-bold mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">Your project stays the anchor</div>
        <p class="text-slate text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The session runs inside its CWD, and new messages continue to target that project until you decide to switch.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-terminal border border-slate-dark rounded-xl p-6">
        <div class="text-cyber font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-bold mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">No disposable remote shell</div>
        <p class="text-slate text-sm leading-relaxed">
          NightMe is built around persistent agent sessions, not one-off commands that vanish when the connection closes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-terminal border border-slate-dark rounded-xl p-6">
        <div class="text-cyber font-mono text-[10px] sm:text-xs font-bold mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">You own the lifecycle</div>
        <p class="text-slate text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Start, stop, steer, and continue the work yourself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section id="agents" class="py-16 sm:py-24 bg-night border-b border-slate-dark">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center mb-10 sm:mb-14">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-terminal border border-slate-dark text-xs font-mono text-cyber mb-4 uppercase tracking-wider">
        Task-fit agents + harnesses
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-6">
        Choose the agent + harness that fits the work.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate max-w-3xl mx-auto text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Different tasks need different execution environments. Use the agent and harness that best fit the work—Claude Code for coding, Codex for writing, Pi for other workflows—while keeping the same NightMe conversation and control experience.
      </p>
    </div>

    
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-10 sm:mb-12">
      <div class="bg-terminal border border-slate-dark rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="h-9 bg-night border-b border-slate-dark flex items-center px-4 gap-2">
          <div class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-alert"></div>
